// uax15_tests.nv — the normalisation conformance clause, run whole.
//
// `NormalizationTest.txt` is five columns of codepoints per line — a
// source, and its NFC, NFD, NFKC and NFKD — and UAX #15's conformance
// clause is the twenty equalities they imply:
//
//     NFC(c1)  = NFC(c2)  = NFC(c3)  = c2
//     NFC(c4)  = NFC(c5)  = c4
//     NFD(c1)  = NFD(c2)  = NFD(c3)  = c3
//     NFD(c4)  = NFD(c5)  = c5
//     NFKC(c1) = NFKC(c2) = NFKC(c3) = NFKC(c4) = NFKC(c5) = c4
//     NFKD(c1) = NFKD(c2) = NFKD(c3) = NFKD(c4) = NFKD(c5) = c5
//
// Every one of them is checked, on every case.
//
// The sample below is committed so `novo test` proves conformance with
// no download; the whole file — twenty thousand cases — runs through
// the same reader when `NOVO_UCD` names a directory holding it:
//
//     NOVO_UCD=/path/to/ucd novo test tests/uax15_tests.nv

use std.env
use std.fs
use std.list
use std.str
use std.test
use udata
use unorm

